-// Decide whether to hesitate, and say why.
-//
-// THE MEASUREMENT CAME FIRST AND IT INVERTED THE OBVIOUS FIX. A player
-// on dm4 pauses 21.9 times per 185 s for 26.5 s in total, a mean of
-// 1.20 s per pause (eleven reference tracks, --profile on the human
-// corpus). Bots already pause 18 to 24 times - the COUNT was never
-// wrong. They pause for 14 to 17 s in total, because each stop is a
-// 0.6 s brake-and-go. So the gap is not missing pauses to insert, it
-// is existing pauses that end too early, and a design that inserted
-// fresh stops would have overshot the fraction while never touching
-// the mean. (It also would have handed out free kills: every inserted
-// stop is a new occasion to be shot standing still, where a lengthened
-// one is not.)
-//
-// Hence two cases, weighted the way the numbers ask:
-//
-//   settle    the common one. The bot has just come off gait speed for
-//             its own reasons - a corner, an arrival, a deflection -
-//             and instead of snapping straight back to 320 it takes
-//             the beat a player takes. Adds no stop, lengthens one.
-//   heard     the rare, legible one. Something fired or was taken out
-//             of sight, far enough off to be news rather than a fight
-//             already lost, so the bot stops and looks at it. The
-//             glance at a sound has existed since the ears slice and
-//             never once broke stride.
-//   junction  likewise rare: the hop after the one being walked turns
-//             hard, so the bot stops at the corner and looks round it
-//             before committing.
